Wait: the push-out when dx is 0 (center inside horizontally): `b.x += (dx>=0?1:-1)*(b.r - 0 + 1)` pushes right by r+1. Fine.

But subtle bug: after breaking a brick and breaking out of the loop, the ball may still overlap another brick — next substep handles it. OK.

Also paddle check `b.y + b.r <= paddle.y + paddle.h + 12` — with substeps ≤6px, ball bottom crosses paddle top within a few px; tolerance 12 is fine. But if ball is below paddle (already passed), condition y+r <= paddle.y+h+12 prevents re-bounce from below. OK.

